cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use nonius, please cite it as below."
title: "nonius: a benchmark composer and composability audit"
abstract: >-
  nonius composes a benchmark's own already-committed items into depth-graded composites
  whose gold is a deterministic function of the component golds, computed by the
  benchmark's own execution oracle, with no examiner and no new items. It also declines:
  a free pre-flight audit reports whether an item set can be composed at all and how far,
  on the grounds that type-compatible substitutions are usually not live ones.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ji
    given-names: Yuxiang
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9835-3800"
    affiliation: "Sunway College"
    alias: KurathSec
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/KurathSec/nonius"
keywords:
  - benchmark saturation
  - evaluation
  - metamorphic testing
  - compositional difficulty
  - execution oracle
# version and date-released are deliberately absent: an archival service supplies them per
# release, and a hand-maintained copy here would only drift.
references:
